id: pmc-sdk-host-alignment-1122
title: Adopt pm-cli 2026.11.24 and refresh pm-changelog tooling
description: "Companion: pm-cli-website-spus. Verify the stale Dependabot changelog failure against main, adopt the current pm-cli host and pm-ops pins, and keep published dependency bullets in changelog generation and release notes."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: sdk-migration
created_at: "2026-11-24T18:59:29.656Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T20:04:27.676Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Pin the latest released toolchain and verify SDK behaviour on real trackers; Preserve published dependency notes and guard the changelog entry points; Pass focused local gates and submit the migration for the CI matrix
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T19:26:58.097Z",codex-agent,"Current main at 10fa503 passed changelog:check with the previous pins. Dependabot PRs #368, #371, #372, and #373 each passed 1,171 tests, then failed changelog:check because their own dependency bump added an Unreleased bullet. The #369 toolchain job stopped at CI health before tests: the old filter recognized the combined stale-work warning and the new host also reports idle and unowned work. Both CI filters now admit those two advisory counts and still require the exact historical provenance baseline. Each actual filter passes the real health result, fails when reverted, and rejects five unsupported health inputs.\n\nThe initial full SDK run passed 1,167 of 1,172 tests with zero skips. Its five failures were custom-type enumeration, entry-from, dependency grouping, missing requested releases, and itemless dependency release notes. The old harness forwarded generate-only flags to export. The new host refuses those flags before dispatch with unknown_option and exit 2. Keep each existing assertion against documented command options and add a negative check for all four invalid flags. The previous and current published SDKs reproduced acceptance and refusal. The final nine affected files passed 62 of 62 tests.\n\nGeneration and release notes explicitly request dependency updates. The check inherits the same generation arguments. Removing either flag or bypassing check delegation failed the regression before restoration. Regeneration retained the published changelog byte-for-byte and all 33 dependency sections. Node 26 build, typecheck, test build, docstring lint (303 declarations), 115-file pack privacy scan, prepare, release-notes generation, release-date and attestation checks passed. Full npm and Bun release/coverage gates and packed matrices belong to CI. PR CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/workflows/ci.yml?query=branch%3Adeps%2Fadopt-pm-cli-host-alignment-1122\n"
  "2026-11-24T20:04:27.675Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (Greptile): the widened CI health filter had no committed test. Added test/ci-health-filter.test.ts, which extracts the real jq filter from ci.yml and ci-deep.yml and runs it: the declared advisories pass (including in_progress_unowned and in_progress_idle with positive counts); a zero, non-numeric or suffixed count, a look-alike prefix, an unknown warning, a changed, second or missing frozen provenance warning are all rejected; both tiers must carry the same filter. 3/3 pass."
